From 06101fc82e048390e2cdff8d6620c5304755335f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KawashiroDev <27027367+KawashiroDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: only use WPA_VERSION_3 for SAE with driver SAE
 offload

MediaTek gen4m drivers do SAE through external auth and map an
unknown wpa_versions value to 'no WPA', so with WPA_VERSION_3 they
send a bare auth frame (rejected with status 13), retry as open
system and get deauthenticated. Older wpa_supplicant sent
WPA_VERSION_2 here, which these drivers handle.

Change-Id: Ic7daab36e9b79363aec9410bb15d0585ed37d07d
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
index f8cc9e1..872dd56 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -7015,8 +7015,15 @@ static int nl80211_connect_common(struct wpa_driver_nl80211_data *drv,
 			 * NL80211_ATTR_SAE_PASSWORD is related and was added
 			 * at the same time as NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3.
 			 */
+			/*
+			 * Only drivers that do SAE themselves need to see
+			 * WPA_VERSION_3. External-auth drivers such as MediaTek
+			 * gen4m do not know it and fall back to open auth.
+			 */
 			if (nl80211_attr_supported(drv,
 						   NL80211_ATTR_SAE_PASSWORD) &&
+			    (drv->capa.flags2 &
+			     WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_SAE_OFFLOAD_STA) &&
 			    wpa_key_mgmt_sae(params->key_mgmt_suite))
 				ver |= NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3;
 			else
